# Line endings are settled here rather than left to each person's git config.
#
# Without this, one contributor whose git converts line endings and another whose
# does not will produce commits where every line of a file reads as changed even
# though nothing was really edited, which buries the real change.
#
# "text=auto" normalises to LF inside the repository while leaving each working
# copy to follow that machine's own core.autocrlf preference — so nothing on disk
# has to change, but everyone commits the same thing.
* text=auto

# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe can misparse a .bat that uses LF alone,
# so these keep CRLF in the working copy.
*.bat text eol=crlf
